course: dictionary
lesson: 5317
title: Kelp: the seaweed that makes forests
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Kelp is a large brown seaweed that grows in the sea, often in long ribbons or tall underwater forests. Context gives you the clue: «Sea otters eat sea urchins, and sea urchins eat kelp seaweed.» Kelp is something urchins eat, and the words "seaweed" next to it tell you what kind of thing it is.
explain: Kelp can also mean seaweed people use as food or as fertiliser. Fertiliser is something spread on soil to help plants grow. Check by swapping in your meaning: "sea urchins eat a large brown seaweed" still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
explain: Kelp is not a true plant. It is a kind of algae that makes its food from sunlight, but it grows like a plant, which is why it is easy to mistake for one.
fact: Kelp is a large brown seaweed that grows in the sea.
fact: «Kelp forests» are tall underwater forests of kelp, and they give homes and food to fish, crabs and sea otters.
fact: «A strand of kelp» means one long piece or ribbon of kelp.
fact: Kelp grows in cool seas, such as off California, Canada, Tasmania and New Zealand.
fact: Kelp is a kind of algae, not a true plant, but it makes its food from sunlight.
exercise: «Sea otters eat sea urchins, and sea urchins eat kelp seaweed.» What is kelp in this sentence? | *A kind of seaweed that sea urchins eat | A kind of fish | A rock on the sea floor | An animal that eats sea otters
exercise: What is a «kelp forest»? | *Tall underwater forests made of kelp | A group of trees on a beach | A crowd of people on a ship | A dry field of wheat
exercise: Which of these is a use for kelp? | Fuel for aeroplanes | *Food or fertiliser | Paint for walls | Building bricks for houses
test: «Steller's sea cow was found in 1741 near islands in the far north Pacific, was up to about eight metres long and ate kelp.» What did Steller's sea cow eat? | Rocks | *Kelp | Fish | Sea urchins
test: Where does kelp grow best, according to the facts? | *Cool seas | Dry fields | Mountain lakes | Hot desert sand
exam: «Sea otters eat sea urchins, which eat kelp, so otters protect kelp forests.» Why do sea otters protect kelp forests? | They eat the kelp so the forest grows bigger | They float on rocks to keep the forest cool | They sleep in the kelp and cut it down | *They eat sea urchins, which would otherwise eat the kelp
